\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Reuters and Associated Press \par \uc2 450 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AUTOMOTIVE\par \par \uc2 Automakers Ask Congress To Block Chinese Rivals\par \par \uc2 Major automakers on Thursday urged Washington to prevent Chinese government-backed automakers and battery manufacturers from opening U.S. manufacturing plants, warning the industry's future is at stake.\par \par \uc2 The Alliance for Automotive Innovation, which represents \uc2 General Motors\uc2 , Ford, \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2 , \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2 , Hyundai, \uc2 Stellantis\uc2  and others, said Congress needed to act.\par \par \uc2 ''China poses a clear and present threat to the auto industry in the U.S.,'' the group wrote in a statement for a House hearing on Chinese vehicles. It also said lawmakers should keep the Commerce Department's ban on importing information and communications technology from China.\par \par \uc2 ''No amount of investment by automakers and battery manufacturers operating inside the U.S. can counter a China that is enabled by subsidies to chronically oversupply around the world,'' the group said. Reuters\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Unemployment Claims Surged, Labor Dept. Says\par \par \uc2 The number of Americans filing new applications for unemployment benefits increased by the most in nearly 4 and a half years last week, but the surge likely does not suggest a material weakening in labor market conditions, because the claims data are volatile around this time of year.\par \par \uc2 The larger-than-expected rise in initial weekly jobless claims reported by the Labor Department on Thursday reversed the sharp drop in the prior week, which had pushed filings to a three-year low.\par \par \uc2 Economists said adjusting the data for seasonal fluctuations is always a challenge, and recommended focusing on the four-week moving average to get a better read of the labor market. The four-week average suggested the labor market was stable.\par \par \uc2 ''The bulk of this week-to-week volatility is seasonal noise,'' said \uc2 Stephen Stanley\uc2 , chief U.S. economist at Santander U.S. Capital Markets. Reuters\par \par \uc2 FISHING\par \par \uc2 Moratorium on Catching Shrimp Is Extended\par \par \uc2 Regulators voted on Thursday to extend a shutdown preventing New England fishermen from catching shrimp, a historic industry that has recently fallen victim to warming oceans.\par \par \uc2 New England fishermen, especially those from Maine, used to catch millions of pounds of small pink shrimp in the winter, but the business has been under a fishing moratorium since 2014. Rising temperatures have created an inhospitable environment for the shrimp, and their population is too low to fish, scientists have said.\par \par \uc2 An arm of the regulatory \uc2 Atlantic States Marine Fisheries Commission\uc2  voted Thursday to shut down the fishery for at least another three years. Abundance of the shrimp remained ''poor'' this year despite slightly improved environmental conditions, the Atlantic States said in documents.\par \par \uc2 The decision came after an industry-funded sampling caught only 70 shrimp totaling less than 3 pounds. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020251212elcc00052\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
