\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Paramount To Lay Off Thousands Of Workers\b0\par\par\uc2 By Benjamin Mullin \par \uc2 404 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 6\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The job cuts are the result of a merger with \uc2 Skydance\uc2  , the Hollywood studio founded by \uc2 David Ellison\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Paramount on Wednesday began laying off more than 2,000 employees, a long-awaited consequence of its merger with the Hollywood studio Skydance.\par \par \uc2 The cuts, announced internally by \uc2 David Ellison\uc2  , Paramount's chief executive, will initially include roughly 1,000 employees in the United States across many divisions, including CBS News, the Paramount film studio and cable networks like \uc2 MTV\uc2  , Nickelodeon and BET. The rest of the cuts, some of which will affect Paramount's international employees, will come later.\par \par \uc2 Overall, Paramount is planning to cut roughly 10 percent of the combined company.\par \par \uc2 In a memo to employees Wednesday, Mr. Ellison said that the cuts were focused on eliminating redundant jobs or phasing out positions not in keeping with Paramount's evolving priorities.\par \par \uc2 ''These decisions are never made lightly, especially given their effect on our colleagues who have made meaningful contributions to the company,'' Mr. Ellison said in the memo.\par \par \uc2 Paramount employees, who have been subjected to near-annual corporate reorganizations, have been bracing for layoffs for months. When \uc2 Skydance\uc2  announced its merger with Paramount last year, the company said it was looking for $2 billion in synergies, Wall Street argot for cost-cutting.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Ellison signaled earlier this year that major changes were coming. In September, he sent a memo telling employees they would be expected to return to the office five days a week in the coming months. Employees unwilling or unable to return to the office would be eligible for a severance package, he said.\par \par \uc2 Some of Paramount's most senior employees have already announced their departures as the layoffs have drawn near. Pam Kaufman, the head of Paramount's international business, told employees in September she was leaving after more than a quarter-century. Chris Aronson, the president of U.S. distribution for \uc2 Paramount Pictures\uc2  , said this month that he would be departing in December.\par \par \uc2 Successive waves of layoffs have become the new normal in Hollywood as executives merge companies and try to wring out billions in costs after those deals close. The specter of further cuts has been the talk of Hollywood in recent days as Mr. Ellison plans a bid for \uc2 Warner Bros. Discovery\uc2  , the parent company of CNN, \uc2 HBO\uc2  and the \uc2 Warner Bros.\uc2  film studio.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020251030elau0003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
