\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 UPS\uc2  Has Cut 48,000 Employees Since Last Year\b0\par\par\uc2 By Peter Eavis \par \uc2 565 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 5\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 About 70 percent of the layoffs affected drivers and warehouse workers, the delivery company said.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  has since last year reduced its work force by 48,000 employees, the company said on Tuesday, in a cost-cutting drive aimed at bolstering profits and winning back investors.\par \par \uc2 The Atlanta-based delivery company, which had nearly half a million employees at the start of the year, said 34,000 positions were cut this year among its drivers and warehouse workers, mostly in the United States. The other 14,000 came out of management's ranks in cuts that began last year.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2 's stock price has long lagged the wider stock market, putting pressure on its leaders to deliver stronger profits. News of the work force reductions and better-than-expected third-quarter results prompted a 7 percent jump in the company's shares on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 ''We are executing the most significant strategic shift in our company's history, and the changes we are implementing are designed to deliver long-term value for all stakeholders,'' \uc2 Carol Tom\u233\'00\'E9\uc2 , \uc2 UPS\uc2 's chief executive, said in a news release.\par \par \uc2 Employment has stalled across the economy, according to the latest government data. And other companies are also shrinking their work forces. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  is planning to cut 14,000 white-collar jobs, a company memo said, to reduce bureaucracy and shift resources.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  reported net income of $1.3 billion in the third quarter, down from $1.5 billion a year earlier. Revenue totaled $21.4 billion in the third quarter, a decline from $22.2 billion last year.\par \par \uc2 Though profit declined, \uc2 UPS\uc2  executives pointed to improvements elsewhere in the results on a call with Wall Street analysts on Tuesday. Revenue per package in the United States grew 10 percent in the third quarter from a year earlier, Ms. Tom\u233\'00\'E9 said.\par \par \uc2 Many of \uc2 UPS\uc2 's employees are members of the \uc2 Teamsters union\uc2 , which in April warned the company that it would fight job cuts that were not in line with its labor contract. On Tuesday, Ms. Tom\u233\'00\'E9 said \uc2 UPS\uc2  was ''in compliance with the terms of our contract.''\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  spokeswoman did not respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2 's business has also been roiled by the imposition of tariffs this year. The volume of packages sent to the United States from China fell nearly 30 percent in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 President Trump this year closed a loophole that had allowed huge numbers of shipments valued at or below $800, mainly from China, to enter the United States without being subjected to tariffs. After Mr. Trump first closed the loophole for those shipments from mainland China and Hong Kong in May, the flow of packages entering the United States declined sharply, to approximately one million packages a day from some four million previously, Customs and Border Protection said in August.\par \par \uc2 UPS\uc2  delivers parcels for \uc2 Amazon\uc2 , but the company said it had reduced that business because it was not profitable. The company delivered 21 percent fewer \uc2 Amazon\uc2  parcels in the third quarter, compared with last year.\par \par \uc2 Even after Tuesday's rally, \uc2 UPS\uc2 's stock is down by nearly a fourth this year. \uc2 FedEx\uc2 's shares have fallen 11 percent. The S&P 500 index, measuring the performance of large companies, is up 17 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020251029elat00042\par }\page {\par\fs20{\